prompt:
Implement a top-down space shooter using Three.js: the ship is centered at the bottom, with keyboard movement and shooting; enemy waves move downward; lasers destroy enemies in one hit; include particle explosions, lives, and waves.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
// Write your code here
</script>

[View]
(1) Use a top-down camera (for example, positioned on +Y and looking toward the XZ plane), with the ship near the bottom center of the screen; use a dark background or starfield;

[Player]
(2) Use A/D to move along the horizontal axis, consistent with the implementation, and constrain movement to the bottom area;
(3) Press Space to fire a laser: a thin, elongated Mesh that travels upward (+Z or +Y, consistent with the scene) at a speed faster than the enemies;

[Enemy Waves]
(4) Spawn 10 enemies per wave from the top and move them toward the bottom; increment waveNum starting from 1, and optionally increase speed/density;
(5) An enemy is destroyed by 1 laser hit; when destroyed, create a particle burst using Points or multiple small meshes that briefly spread outward;

[Lives]
(6) Initialize lives to 3; when an enemy reaches the bottom or collides with the ship, decrement lives by 1 (use a fixed rule and document it with a comment); when lives=0, the game ends and input may be frozen;

[Score]
(7) Increase score when an enemy is destroyed (the exact point value is up to you and must be written to __3D_STATE__);

[UI]
(8) Include id="score", id="lives", and id="wave";

[State Exposure (Required)]
(9) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame with:
  - score, lives, waveNum, enemiesAlive, shipPos:{x,y,z}, shotsFired

[Evaluation Helpers (Recommended)]
(10) window.__STATEPROBE_destroyOneEnemy__() immediately destroys one enemy, applying the same score increase and particles as a real kill; window.__STATEPROBE_damagePlayer__() simulates losing one life.

Output a single HTML file that runs when opened directly in a browser.
